From 87e5d6b002e8de9276806a2286fa1b52054c1d8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:44:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luks: prevent user-buffer deadlocks and protect destructive
 commands

Wire user buffers before taking the volume lock or a bounce buffer. Page
faults can reenter the same encrypted volume: sixteen concurrent reads
into cold private file mappings exhausted the original four-buffer pool
and completed zero reads. The fixed driver completes all sixteen.

Flush regular-file backing with fsync rather than accepting an unsupported
device ioctl. Count only supported, bound, non-ignored keyslots when
protecting the last automatically usable slot. Compare copy endpoints
before truncating an output, including hard-link and symlink aliases.

Add eight host safety checks and a native QEMU memory regression. The
optimized interoperability/crash suite passes 69 checks; the safety cases
pass optimized and ASan/UBSan builds (leak detection disabled because of
the traced environment). The native driver, CLI and helper cross-compile
and link, and the QEMU regression completes 16/16 reads with no errors.

AI-written with OpenAI Codex for the repository owner.
